diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index f53d2fc6e..f8de10f89 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -110,3 +110,9 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - ci: npx -y uw-harness verify returned 404 from the npm registry on 2026-11-01 (package not published). The new harness.yml workflow will fail until uw-harness is published; it was not run on GitHub. Locally the check was run with the uw-harness source checkout and passed.
 - local-env: PostgreSQL support (DB_TYPE=pgsql, compose profile pgsql) was written but not run. Only MySQL was verified. The full gate drops and reinstalls the local database each time, and needs host port 3306 free because the mysqli driver ignores other ports.
 - full-gate: The full gate does not build the DocBook guides or the SOAP WSDL HTML (documentation.yml needs Publican and xsltproc, not available as composer/npm dependencies). Everything else from CI (lint, api:validate, api:generate, all four PHPUnit suites) is in composer run check.
+
+## 2026-11-02: global categories in category commands, REST ignores `status` (issue #32470)
+
+- Changed: `CategoryAddCommand`, `CategoryUpdateCommand` and `CategoryDeleteCommand` accept project id 0 (ALL_PROJECTS), with the same check as `CategoryGetCommand`. Delete rules did not change. The commands no longer read a `status` payload field: only `enabled` sets the category status. `status` was removed from the `ProjectCategoriesAdd` and `ProjectCategoriesUpdate` schemas in `api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml`. Tests added in `tests/Mantis/CategoryCommandTest.php`, `tests/Mantis/CategoryDeleteCommandTest.php` and `tests/rest/RestProjectCategoryTest.php`.
+- Learned: no SOAP or UI caller passes `status` to the category commands. Only REST payloads could reach it, so removing it does not change SOAP. `helper_parse_id()` rejects 0, so ALL_PROJECTS must be checked before it is called. `CategoryGetCommand` uses `== ALL_PROJECTS`, which in PHP is also true for a null project id; the new code uses `is_numeric()` and a strict check instead. `composer run check` stops the web server when it ends, so to run REST tests with `--filter` after it, use `build/local_instance.sh test --filter ...`.
+- Left: `CategoryGetCommand` still treats a missing `project_id` as ALL_PROJECTS (loose comparison). Not changed here.
